      "content": "It can be incredibly painful and demoralizing to experience a complete creative drying-up, especially when it feels like it's all you've ever been able to do. Not wanting to continue and risk becoming a caricature of your former self is a valid concern, and it's natural to feel overwhelmed by the prospect of being a shadow of your former self. It might be helpful to take a step back and acknowledge that it's okay to confront the end of a chapter, even if it's a difficult or uncomfortable one.",
      "source": "target",
